1
00:05:23,478 --> 00:05:29,478
There is no justice, there is only revenge.

2
00:10:46,956 --> 00:10:52,956
The Punisher is a action, crime, drama film directed by Jonathan Hensleigh.

3
00:16:10,434 --> 00:16:16,434
When undercover FBI agent Frank Castle's wife and son are slaughtered, he becomes 'the
Punisher' -- a ruthless vigilante willing to go to any length to avenge his family.

4
00:21:33,913 --> 00:21:39,913
Frank Castle / The Punisher, played by Thomas Jane.

5
00:26:57,391 --> 00:27:03,391
Howard Saint, played by John Travolta.

6
00:32:20,869 --> 00:32:26,869
Quentin Glass, played by Will Patton.

7
00:37:44,347 --> 00:37:50,347
Frank Castle, Sr., played by Roy Scheider.

8
00:43:07,826 --> 00:43:13,826
Livia Saint, played by Laura Harring.

9
00:48:31,304 --> 00:48:37,304
Specker Dave, played by Ben Foster.

10
00:53:54,782 --> 00:54:00,782
The Punisher is a 2004 vigilante action film based on the Marvel Comics character of the same name, directed by
Jonathan Hensleigh, in his directorial debut, who also co-wrote the film with Michael France.

11
00:59:18,260 --> 00:59:24,260
It stars Thomas Jane as the antihero Frank Castle and John Travolta as Howard
Saint, a crime boss who orders the deaths of Castle's entire family.

12
01:04:41,739 --> 01:04:47,739
The film's story and plot were mainly based on two Punisher comic book stories: the 1994 miniseries The Punisher: Year One, by writers Dan Abnett and Andy Lanning, and the 2000–01 miniseries Welcome Back, Frank, by writer Garth
Ennis, though some scenes were derived from other Punisher stories, such as Marvel Preview Presents: The Punisher #2, Marvel Super Action Featuring: The Punisher #1, The Punisher War Zone, and The Punisher War Journal.

13
01:10:05,217 --> 01:10:11,217
The Punisher was shot on location in Tampa, Florida,
and environs in mid- to late 2003.

14
01:15:28,695 --> 01:15:34,695
It was distributed by Lions Gate Films in North America, although Artisan Entertainment, which released a 1989 film
adaptation of the same name on DVD, financed and co-distributed the film with eventual Artisan owner Lionsgate.

15
01:20:52,173 --> 01:20:58,173
Artisan's sales agent Summit Entertainment handled international sales, with Columbia TriStar Film Distributors International acquiring the rights
in all non-North American territories except for eight Southeast Asian and Middle East territories, as well as India and China.

16
01:26:15,652 --> 01:26:21,652
Screenwriter Jonathan Hensleigh agreed to direct the film during its development stage,
despite a dispute with Marvel Studios, marking his directorial debut.

17
01:31:39,130 --> 01:31:45,130
Lionsgate Films released The Punisher on April 16, 2004.

18
01:37:02,608 --> 01:37:08,608
It received generally negative reviews and grossed $13 million in the United States over its opening
weekend; it reached a total gross of $54.7 million against a budget of $33 million.

19
01:42:26,086 --> 01:42:32,086
Marvel Comics and Lionsgate began development on a sequel titled The Punisher 2, which instead became the 2008
reboot Punisher: War Zone after Jane and Hensleigh left the project due to creative differences.

20
01:47:49,565 --> 01:47:55,565
The film marks the final production by Artisan
Entertainment for theatrical distribution.

21
01:53:13,043 --> 01:53:19,043
The film explores themes of undercover, submachine
gun, chain, superhero, twin brother.

22
01:58:36,521 --> 01:58:42,521
The tone is emotional.
